To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 2 other than $a_{21}=-3$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\ -3 & 6 & 3 & -6 \\ 3 & -4 & 6 & 0 \\ -3 & 3 & 9 & -8\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}+2C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 0 & 5 \\ -3 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\ 3 & 2 & 6 & 0 \\ -3 & -3 & 9 & -8\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\ -3 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\ 3 & 2 & 9 & 0 \\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -8\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{4}:=C_{4}-2C_{1}}\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & 3 & -1 \\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\ 3 & 2 & 9 & -6 \\ -3 & -3 & 6 & -2\end{bmatrix}=B
$$

Therefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are

$C_{2}:=C_{2}+2C_{1}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+C_{1}$.

